Package: adc-crt-control
Version: 3.0.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Roasted-Codes <Roasted-Codes@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0
Recommends: i2c-tools
Conflicts: pi-adc-control
Replaces: pi-adc-control
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Roasted-Codes/ad-crt-control
Description: control an Apple Studio Display 17" CRT through an ADC adapter
 Power, geometry calibration, degauss and save-to-NVRAM for the Apple Studio
 Display 17" CRT (M7768) connected through the Jason "Does It All" ADC
 adapter. Monitor state and geometry go over USB HID. Power is set over
 DDC/CI, either on the graphics card's display connector or, on a Raspberry
 Pi, on GPIO I2C bus 1 wired to the adapter's DVI port.
 .
 Provides the adc-crt command (command line, GTK 3 window, and a listener for
 the monitor's front-panel button), a udev rule that gives the logged-in user
 access without sudo, and a boot service that powers the monitor on.
 .
 Replaces pi-adc-control 2.x and removes the empty labwc keybinding it left
 behind in /etc/xdg/labwc/rc.xml.
